cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "paddleocr-hebrew: production Hebrew OCR with a script-gated CTC/attention cascade"
message: "If you use these models or the findings, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Rivok Labs"
    website: "https://rivoklabs.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rivoklabs/paddleocr-hebrew"
url: "https://huggingface.co/rivoklabs/paddleocr-hebrew"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-29"
keywords:
  - Hebrew
  - OCR
  - optical character recognition
  - right-to-left
  - bidirectional text
  - BiDi
  - CTC
  - attention decoder
  - SVTRv2
  - PaddleOCR
  - ONNX
abstract: >-
  A family of Hebrew OCR models finetuned from PaddleOCR, released as ONNX under
  Apache-2.0, together with a runnable page pipeline. The central finding is that a
  monotonic CTC decoder blank-collapses Latin and digit runs embedded inside
  right-to-left Hebrew, deleting them entirely rather than misreading them, while an
  attention decoder on the same backbone reads them natively. The release deploys this
  as a confidence- and script-gated CTC-to-attention cascade, obtaining attention-level
  quality on mixed-script text at approximately CTC latency.
